      "currency": "GBP",
      "description": "Ripple Player is a record player for the albums in your Apple Music library. Albums, front to back.\n\nYour whole albums stand on a shelf as record spines, each one made from its own sleeve. Pull one out, put it on, and it plays from the first track to the last, with nothing queued up behind it. No shuffle, no playlists, no feed.\n\nPUT A RECORD ON\n• The arm moves across the record as it plays, so you can see how far in you are.\n• Lift the needle and set it down on another track.\n• When the album ends, the needle settles into the run-out groove and the arm goes home.\n\nTURN IT OVER FOR THE TRACKS\nTap the playing sleeve and it turns over to its back: the track list, set like a real sleeve. Ten tracks or sixty, the back always fits.\n\nONLY WHOLE ALBUMS\nYour shelf holds the albums you've saved in full. Save a whole album, or add one straight from Ripple Player's search, and it takes its place on the shelf. A switch in Settings shows singles and part-saved albums too.\n\nWATER THAT HEARS THE MUSIC\nThe turntable floats on dark water, with your shelf reflected on the surface. If you let it, the water ripples with the music, listening only while a record plays. Nothing is recorded and nothing leaves your phone.\n\nMADE FOR IPHONE DUO\nOpen it like a laptop: the shelf stands up, the turntable lies flat, and the water reflects your records as the hinge moves. Close it on the record and it keeps playing under a glass lid. It works on every iPhone too.\n\nYOURS ALONE\nNo account, no ads, no tracking. Ripple Player collects no data.\n\nWorks with Apple Music only. An Apple Music subscription is needed to play most albums.\n\nApple and Apple Music are trademarks of Apple Inc., registered in the U.S. and other countries.",
